  :1-g7h8i9
  {:statement
   "Define $Z_S = \\bigotimes_{i=1}^n P_i$ where $P_i = Z$ if $i \\in S$ and $P_i = I$ otherwise. This is a diagonal Pauli operator with eigenvalues $\\pm 1$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "f20f83144085ccba",
   :display-order 3,
   :type :definition,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :definition-expansion,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-g7h8i9,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{}},
  :1-j1k2l3
  {:statement
   "For all $x \\in \\{0,1\\}^n$ and $S \\subseteq [n]$, we have $\\langle x | Z_S | x \\rangle = (-1)^{\\sum_{i \\in S} x_i} = \\chi_S(x)$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "029c9a3cf87cb9cb",
   :display-order 4,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-j1k2l3,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-g7h8i9}},
  :2-m4n5o6
  {:statement
   "Proof of $\\langle x | Z_S | x \\rangle = \\chi_S(x)$: Since $Z = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}$, we have $\\langle x_i | Z | x_i \\rangle = (-1)^{x_i}$ for each qubit. For $i \\in S$, the $Z_S$ operator has $Z$ at position $i$, and $\\langle x_i | Z | x_i \\rangle = (-1)^{x_i}$. For $i \\notin S$, $Z_S$ has $I$, and $\\langle x_i | I | x_i \\rangle = 1$. By tensor product structure, $\\langle x | Z_S | x \\rangle = \\prod_{i \\in S} (-1)^{x_i} = (-1)^{\\sum_{i \\in S} x_i} = \\chi_S(x)$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent :1-j1k2l3,
   :content-hash "0a33ea6d5fc89685",
   :display-order 5,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :2-m4n5o6,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 2,
   :dependencies #{:1-j1k2l3 :1-g7h8i9}},
  :1-p7q8r9
  {:statement
   "For the operator $\\sum_{S \\subseteq [n]} \\hat{f}(S) Z_S$, the diagonal matrix element is $\\langle x | \\sum_{S} \\hat{f}(S) Z_S | x \\rangle = \\sum_{S} \\hat{f}(S) \\chi_S(x) = f(x)$ by the Fourier expansion of $f$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "b99875a7baaf22da",
   :display-order 6,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :substitution,
